se,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"grade\":\"partial\",\"rationale\":\"Correct central content: the fixed fee covers processing, transfer agent and custody settlement costs. The variable fee covers trading-related costs (brokerage, taxes, spreads, market impact) and protects remaining shareholders from dilution. The answer correctly says the AP bears both fees and correctly treats them as cost recovery distinct from AP compensation, avoiding the barred claim that the fee reimburses the AP. Substantive problems: (1) Recipient error. It says transaction fees are 'paid into the fund' and that service providers are paid from fund expenses. This contradicts the key point that fixed charges may go to the custodian or another service provider while variable charges go to the fund, as in the Corgi SAI. Its statement that 'recipients can differ' concerns fund charges versus AP compensation, not fixed versus variable fees. (2) It omits waivers entirely: no mention that the AP bears the charge unless it is waived or paid by another party, and no mention of the observation that sponsors often waive custom-redemption charges. (3) It only weakly emphasizes that variable charges apply particularly to cash, partial-cash or non-standard orders.\"}","ttft_ms":2995,"type":"result","duration_ms":6256,"uuid":"198c216f-249c-472b-ad71-be1a007d4a30","ttft_stream_ms":568,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":568,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
